  {
   "id": "concept2",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "NAND (active-low) SR latch"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "Two cross-coupled NAND gates also make a latch, but its inputs are active-low ($\\bar{S}$ and $\\bar{R}$). $\\bar{S}$ = 0 sets Q = 1, $\\bar{R}$ = 0 resets Q = 0, $\\bar{S} = \\bar{R}$ = 1 holds, and $\\bar{S} = \\bar{R}$ = 0 is invalid (it forces Q = $\\bar{Q}$ = 1). A common use of the latch is a switch debouncer, which removes the extra pulses produced when a mechanical switch bounces."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "NAND latch inputs are active-low"
    },
    {
     "en": "S̄ = R̄ = 1: hold; S̄ = R̄ = 0: invalid"
    },
    {
     "en": "Use: switch debouncing"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "With NAND gates the inputs are active low: a zero sets or resets. Both inputs high hold the state, and both low is the forbidden case.",
    "kn": "NAND ಲ್ಯಾಚ್‌ನಲ್ಲಿ ಇನ್‌ಪುಟ್‌ಗಳು ಸಕ್ರಿಯ-ಕಡಿಮೆ: 0 ಸೆಟ್ ಅಥವಾ ರೀಸೆಟ್ ಮಾಡುತ್ತದೆ. ಎರಡೂ 1 ಹಿಂದಿನ ಸ್ಥಿತಿ ಉಳಿಸುತ್ತದೆ; ಎರಡೂ 0 ನಿಷಿದ್ಧ."
   }
  },
