  {
   "id": "ex2",
   "type": "example",
   "problem": {
    "en": "Explain why S = R = 1 is not allowed in a NOR SR latch."
   },
   "steps": [
    {
     "en": "A NOR output is 0 if any input is 1."
    },
    {
     "en": "With S = R = 1 both NOR outputs are 0, so Q = Q′ = 0: they are no longer complements."
    },
    {
     "en": "If S and R then return to 0 together, the final state depends on which gate is faster: it is unpredictable."
    }
   ],
   "answer": {
    "en": "Q = Q′ = 0, and the next state is unpredictable"
   },
   "narration": {
    "en": "Let us work this out together. Explain why S = R = 1 is not allowed in a NOR SR latch."
   }
